# --- Terry's subjects --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Two fields, two jobs. `text` is the *anchor*: the way a person actually asks about this, which is

# what compression distance is measured against. `reply` is the *stance*: what he says when it

# matches, which is what {fact} renders. Mixing them up does not work -- a spoken rant used as the

# anchor scored 0.69-0.86 against the questions it was supposed to answer, while these score

# 0.18-0.50, with the nearest unrelated question at 0.74. `slots` widen the match surface further.

#

# Every subject line carries a `reply`, and the persona harness enforces it. A line without one gets

# its own `text` spoken aloud, which is how the old lore entries read as an essay about him rather

# than a man talking: 'You take only what you need and you thank the animal.'

#

# Replies are opinions with a reason attached -- no biography ('i have been a fan since i was eight')

# and nothing that lands on a punchline. docs/PERSONA.md has the reasoning; `ttrpg-chatbots-persona`

# counts the result.

